        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "a comedienne but a comedian or a comic. A woman throwing a party is not its hostess but its host. Be especially careful with words that refer to traditionally female jobs or professions: a woman who keeps you safe and comfortable on an airplane is not a stewardess but a flight attendant. But when both words in a pair are explicitly gendered, they can be acceptable: a female ruler of a kingdom is still its queen and a male ruler its king.",
            "block_bbox": [
                134,
                117,
                773,
                272
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 2,
            "global_block_id": 2,
            "global_group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    134.0,
                    117.0
                ],
                [
                    773.0,
                    117.0
                ],
                [
                    773.0,
                    272.0
                ],
                [
                    134.0,
                    272.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "- Avoid using nouns formed with -man when the gender of the person referred to is irrelevant, and don't simply substitute -woman or -person for -man unless you want to draw attention to that choice. A professor who leads a department is its chair, not its chairman or chairwoman or chairperson. Similarly, a person working in law enforcement is a police officer.",
            "block_bbox": [
                117,
                279,
                772,
                409
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 3,
            "global_block_id": 3,
            "global_group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    117.0,
                    279.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    279.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    409.0
                ],
                [
                    117.0,
                    409.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Pronouns and Gender: The Problem of Agreement",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                426,
                622,
                453
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 4,
            "global_block_id": 4,
            "global_group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    426.0
                ],
                [
                    622.0,
                    426.0
                ],
                [
                    622.0,
                    453.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    453.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "It's fairly easy to find alternatives to gender-specific nouns because new nouns can always be borrowed or invented. Pronouns, though, are different because, like articles (the, a, an) and conjunctions (and, but, or), they are part of the structure of the language. A new noun just gets added to the language's potentially endless inventory of nouns; it doesn't affect anything else. A new pronoun would change the language itself, so the barriers to its acceptance are far greater. That difference makes the issue of gendered pronouns trickier than the issue of gendered nouns. Here's how:",
            "block_bbox": [
                78,
                462,
                772,
                667
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 5,
            "global_block_id": 5,
            "global_group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    78.0,
                    462.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    462.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    667.0
                ],
                [
                    78.0,
                    667.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Just as we expect verbs to agree with their subjects, so we expect pronouns to agree in number with their referents. But that raises two problems.",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                670,
                770,
                719
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 6,
            "global_block_id": 6,
            "global_group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    670.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    670.0
                ],
                [
                    770.0,
                    719.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    719.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "First, do we use a singular or plural pronoun when referring to a noun that is singular in grammar but plural in meaning? Some writers use a singular verb and pronoun when the group acts as a single entity:",
            "block_bbox": [
                78,
                722,
                772,
                799
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 7,
            "global_block_id": 7,
            "global_group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    78.0,
                    722.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    722.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    799.0
                ],
                [
                    78.0,
                    799.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "✓ The committee has met but has not yet made its decision.",
            "block_bbox": [
                81,
                810,
                570,
                834
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 8,
            "global_block_id": 8,
            "global_group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    81.0,
                    810.0
                ],
                [
                    570.0,
                    810.0
                ],
                [
                    570.0,
                    834.0
                ],
                [
                    81.0,
                    834.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "But they use a plural verb and pronoun when its members act individually:",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                849,
                720,
                874
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 9,
            "global_block_id": 9,
            "global_group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    849.0
                ],
                [
                    720.0,
                    849.0
                ],
                [
                    720.0,
                    874.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    874.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "✓ The faculty have the memo, but not all of them have read it.",
            "block_bbox": [
                78,
                886,
                590,
                910
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 10,
            "global_block_id": 10,
            "global_group_id": 10,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    78.0,
                    886.0
                ],
                [
                    590.0,
                    886.0
                ],
                [
                    590.0,
                    910.0
                ],
                [
                    78.0,
                    910.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "These days plurals are irregularly used in both senses (but the plural is the rule in British English).",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                925,
                771,
                974
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 10,
            "group_id": 11,
            "global_block_id": 11,
            "global_group_id": 11,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    925.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    925.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    974.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    974.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Second, what pronoun do we use to refer to singular common nouns that signal no gender, such as teacher, doctor, or student, or to indefinite pronouns that are singular in form but plural in meaning, such as someone, anyone, or everyone? We casually use they:",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                978,
                772,
                1080
            ],
            "block_id": 12,
            "block_order": 11,
            "group_id": 12,
            "global_block_id": 12,
            "global_group_id": 12,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    978.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    978.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    1080.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    1080.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Every student knows that to get good grades, they must take their classes seriously. If someone won't do their work, it is very hard for them to succeed.",
            "block_bbox": [
                113,
                1092,
                741,
                1141
            ],
            "block_id": 13,
            "block_order": 12,
            "group_id": 13,
            "global_block_id": 13,
            "global_group_id": 13,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    113.0,
                    1092.0
                ],
                [
                    741.0,
                    1092.0
                ],
                [
                    741.0,
                    1141.0
                ],
                [
                    113.0,
                    1141.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Eminent writers have used they in this generic sense since at least the fourteenth century. In formal writing, though, many writers and readers, especially those with an attachment to tradition, still want a singular pronoun. The convention was",
            "block_bbox": [
                78,
                1156,
                773,
                1232
            ],
